{"id":"calculus","name":"Calculus","cards":[{"id":"calculus-1","sides":[{"text":"Definition of a limit","sub":"Beginner · Limits"},{"text":"\\(\\lim_{x\\to a}f(x)=L\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"f(x) gets arbitrarily close to L as x gets close to a (from both sides), whether or not f(a) is defined.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-2","sides":[{"text":"Epsilon-delta definition","sub":"Beginner · Limits"},{"text":"\\(\\forall\\varepsilon>0\\ \\exists\\delta>0:\\ 0<|x-a|<\\delta\\Rightarrow|f(x)-L|<\\varepsilon\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Pick any tolerance on the output; some window around a keeps the output within it.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-3","sides":[{"text":"One-sided limit and existence","sub":"Beginner · Limits"},{"text":"\\(\\lim_{x\\to a}f=L\\iff\\lim_{x\\to a^-}f=\\lim_{x\\to a^+}f=L\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"If the left and right limits differ, the limit does not exist (jump).","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-4","sides":[{"text":"Continuity at a","sub":"Beginner · Limits"},{"text":"\\(\\lim_{x\\to a}f(x)=f(a)\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Three conditions: f(a) exists, the limit exists, and they are equal.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-5","sides":[{"text":"Squeeze theorem","sub":"Beginner · Limits"},{"text":"\\(g\\le f\\le h,\\ \\lim g=\\lim h=L\\Rightarrow\\lim f=L\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Classic use: x sin(1/x) → 0 as x → 0, squeezed between −|x| and |x|.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-6","sides":[{"text":"Intermediate Value Theorem","sub":"Beginner · Limits"},{"text":"f continuous on [a,b], N between f(a) and f(b) ⇒ some c with f(c)=N","sub":"","more":{"text":"Used to prove roots exist, e.g. x³+x−1=0 has a root in (0,1).","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-7","sides":[{"text":"Famous limit: sine","sub":"Beginner · Limits"},{"text":"\\(\\lim_{x\\to0}\\frac{\\sin x}{x}=1\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Angle in radians. Also (1−cos x)/x → 0.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-8","sides":[{"text":"Famous limit: e","sub":"Beginner · Limits"},{"text":"\\(\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\left(1+\\frac1n\\right)^n=e\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Equivalent: lim (1+x)^{1/x} = e as x → 0.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-9","sides":[{"text":"Limit at infinity of a rational function","sub":"Beginner · Limits"},{"text":"Compare degrees of numerator and denominator","sub":"","more":{"text":"Smaller numerator degree → 0. Equal → ratio of leading coefficients. Larger → ±∞.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-10","sides":[{"text":"L'Hôpital's rule","sub":"Beginner · Limits"},{"text":"\\(\\lim\\frac{f}{g}=\\lim\\frac{f'}{g'}\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Only when the limit is 0/0 or ∞/∞. Rewrite 0·∞, ∞−∞, 1^∞ forms first (take logs).","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-11","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\lim_{x\\to 3}\\frac{x^{2} - 9}{x - 3}\\]","sub":"Beginner · Limits","head":"Limit"},{"text":"\\[6\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer","more":{"text":"Direct substitution gives 0/0\nFactor: (x−3)(x+3)/(x−3) = x+3\nAt x=3: 6","sub":"Steps"}}]},{"id":"calculus-12","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{x}\\]","sub":"Beginner · Limits","head":"Limit"},{"text":"\\[3\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer","more":{"text":"Multiply and divide by 3\n3·sin(3x)/(3x) → 3·1","sub":"Steps"}}]},{"id":"calculus-13","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\sqrt{x + 4} - 2}{x}\\]","sub":"Beginner · Limits","head":"Limit"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{4}\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer","more":{"text":"0/0: multiply by the conjugate √(x+4)+2\nNumerator becomes x, which cancels\n1/(√4+2) = 1/4","sub":"Steps"}}]},{"id":"calculus-14","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\lim_{x\\to \\infty}\\frac{3 x^{2} + 2 x}{5 x^{2} - 1}\\]","sub":"Beginner · Limits","head":"Limit"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{3}{5}\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer","more":{"text":"Divide top and bottom by x²\n(3 + 2/x)/(5 − 1/x²) → 3/5","sub":"Steps"}}]},{"id":"calculus-15","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{1 - \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}}{x^{2}}\\]","sub":"Beginner · Limits","head":"Limit"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{2}\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer","more":{"text":"0/0: L'Hôpital gives sin x / 2x\nStill 0/0: gives cos x / 2 → 1/2","sub":"Steps"}}]},{"id":"calculus-16","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{e^{x} - 1}{x}\\]","sub":"Beginner · Limits","head":"Limit"},{"text":"\\[1\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer","more":{"text":"0/0: L'Hôpital gives eˣ/1\nAt 0: 1","sub":"Steps"}}]},{"id":"calculus-17","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\lim_{x\\to \\infty}\\left(1 + \\frac{2}{x}\\right)^{x}\\]","sub":"Beginner · Limits","head":"Limit"},{"text":"\\[e^{2}\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer","more":{"text":"1^∞ form: take ln\nx ln(1+2/x) → 2 (L'Hôpital)\nExponentiate: e²","sub":"Steps"}}]},{"id":"calculus-18","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\lim_{x\\to 0}x \\log{\\left(x \\right)}\\]","sub":"Beginner · Limits","head":"Limit"},{"text":"\\[0\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer","more":{"text":"0·∞: write as ln x / (1/x)\nL'Hôpital: (1/x) / (−1/x²) = −x\n→ 0","sub":"Steps"}}]},{"id":"calculus-19","sides":[{"text":"Definition of the derivative","sub":"Beginner · Derivative rules"},{"text":"\\(f'(x)=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Slope of the tangent line; instantaneous rate of change.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-20","sides":[{"text":"Alternative definition at a","sub":"Beginner · Derivative rules"},{"text":"\\(f'(a)=\\lim_{x\\to a}\\frac{f(x)-f(a)}{x-a}\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"calculus-21","sides":[{"text":"Differentiable ⇒ continuous","sub":"Beginner · Derivative rules"},{"text":"True. The converse is false","sub":"","more":{"text":"|x| is continuous at 0 but has a corner, so no derivative there.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-22","sides":[{"text":"Power rule","sub":"Beginner · Derivative rules"},{"text":"\\(\\frac{d}{dx}x^n=nx^{n-1}\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Holds for any real n.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-23","sides":[{"text":"Constant multiple and sum rules","sub":"Beginner · Derivative rules"},{"text":"\\((cf+g)'=cf'+g'\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"calculus-24","sides":[{"text":"Product rule","sub":"Beginner · Derivative rules"},{"text":"\\((fg)'=f'g+fg'\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"calculus-25","sides":[{"text":"Quotient rule","sub":"Beginner · Derivative rules"},{"text":"\\(\\left(\\frac fg\\right)'=\\frac{f'g-fg'}{g^2}\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Low d-high minus high d-low, over low squared.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-26","sides":[{"text":"Chain rule","sub":"Beginner · Derivative rules"},{"text":"\\(\\frac{d}{dx}f(g(x))=f'(g(x))\\,g'(x)\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Outside derivative at the inside, times the derivative of the inside.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-27","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\sin x\\]","sub":"Beginner · Derivative rules","head":"Derivative"},{"text":"\\[\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer"}]},{"id":"calculus-28","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\cos x\\]","sub":"Beginner · Derivative rules","head":"Derivative"},{"text":"\\[- \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer"}]},{"id":"calculus-29","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\tan x\\]","sub":"Beginner · Derivative rules","head":"Derivative"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{\\cos^{2}{\\left(x \\right)}}\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer"}]},{"id":"calculus-30","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\cot x\\]","sub":"Beginner · Derivative rules","head":"Derivative"},{"text":"\\[- \\frac{1}{\\sin^{2}{\\left(x \\right)}}\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer"}]},{"id":"calculus-31","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\sec x\\]","sub":"Beginner · Derivative rules","head":"Derivative"},{"text":"\\[\\tan{\\left(x \\right)} \\sec{\\left(x \\right)}\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer"}]},{"id":"calculus-32","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\csc x\\]","sub":"Beginner · Derivative rules","head":"Derivative"},{"text":"\\[- \\cot{\\left(x \\right)} \\csc{\\left(x \\right)}\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer"}]},{"id":"calculus-33","sides":[{"text":"\\[e^x\\]","sub":"Beginner · Derivative rules","head":"Derivative"},{"text":"\\[e^{x}\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer"}]},{"id":"calculus-34","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\ln x\\]","sub":"Beginner · Derivative rules","head":"Derivative"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{x}\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer"}]},{"id":"calculus-35","sides":[{"text":"\\[a^x\\]","sub":"Beginner · Derivative rules","head":"Derivative"},{"text":"\\[a^{x} \\ln{\\left(a \\right)}\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer"}]},{"id":"calculus-36","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\log_a x\\]","sub":"Beginner · Derivative rules","head":"Derivative"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{x \\ln{\\left(a \\right)}}\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer"}]},{"id":"calculus-37","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\arcsin x\\]","sub":"Beginner · Derivative rules","head":"Derivative"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - x^{2}}}\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer"}]},{"id":"calculus-38","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\arccos x\\]","sub":"Beginner · Derivative rules","head":"Derivative"},{"text":"\\[- \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - x^{2}}}\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer"}]},{"id":"calculus-39","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\arctan x\\]","sub":"Beginner · Derivative rules","head":"Derivative"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{x^{2} + 1}\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer"}]},{"id":"calculus-40","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\sinh x\\]","sub":"Beginner · Derivative rules","head":"Derivative"},{"text":"\\[\\cosh{\\left(x \\right)}\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer"}]},{"id":"calculus-41","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\cosh x\\]","sub":"Beginner · Derivative rules","head":"Derivative"},{"text":"\\[\\sinh{\\left(x \\right)}\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer"}]},{"id":"calculus-42","sides":[{"text":"Implicit differentiation","sub":"Beginner · Derivative rules"},{"text":"Differentiate both sides w.r.t. x, treat y as y(x), solve for dy/dx","sub":"","more":{"text":"\\(x^2+y^2=25\\Rightarrow\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac xy\\)","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-43","sides":[{"text":"Logarithmic differentiation","sub":"Beginner · Derivative rules"},{"text":"\\(y=f^g\\Rightarrow \\ln y=g\\ln f\\Rightarrow y'=y\\left(g'\\ln f+\\frac{gf'}{f}\\right)\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Use for variable exponents and long products.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-44","sides":[{"text":"Inverse function derivative","sub":"Beginner · Derivative rules"},{"text":"\\((f^{-1})'(b)=\\frac1{f'(a)},\\ f(a)=b\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"calculus-45","sides":[{"text":"\\[x^{3} - 4 x + 1\\]","sub":"Beginner · Derivative problems","head":"Differentiate"},{"text":"\\[3 x^{2} - 4\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer","more":{"text":"Power rule on each term\n3x² − 4 + 0","sub":"Steps"}}]},{"id":"calculus-46","sides":[{"text":"\\[x^{2} e^{x}\\]","sub":"Beginner · Derivative problems","head":"Differentiate"},{"text":"\\[x \\left(x + 2\\right) e^{x}\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer","more":{"text":"Product rule: (x²)′eˣ + x²(eˣ)′\n= 2x eˣ + x² eˣ\n= x(x+2)eˣ","sub":"Steps"}}]},{"id":"calculus-47","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\]","sub":"Beginner · Derivative problems","head":"Differentiate"},{"text":"\\[\\cos2x\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer","more":{"text":"Product rule: cos x·cos x + sin x·(−sin x)\n= cos²x − sin²x = cos 2x","sub":"Steps"}}]},{"id":"calculus-48","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\frac{x^{2} + 1}{x - 1}\\]","sub":"Beginner · Derivative problems","head":"Differentiate"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{x^{2} - 2 x - 1}{\\left(x - 1\\right)^{2}}\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer","more":{"text":"Quotient rule: low d-high − high d-low, over low²\n= [2x(x−1) − (x²+1)] / (x−1)²\n= (x² − 2x − 1) / (x−1)²","sub":"Steps"}}]},{"id":"calculus-49","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\sqrt{x^{2} + 1}\\]","sub":"Beginner · Derivative problems","head":"Differentiate"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x^{2} + 1}}\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer","more":{"text":"Chain rule: outer u^{1/2}, inner x²+1\n= ½(x²+1)^{−1/2} · 2x","sub":"Steps"}}]},{"id":"calculus-50","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\ln{\\left(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} \\right)}\\]","sub":"Beginner · Derivative problems","head":"Differentiate"},{"text":"\\[\\cot x\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer","more":{"text":"Chain rule: (1/sin x) · cos x\n= cot x","sub":"Steps"}}]},{"id":"calculus-51","sides":[{"text":"\\[e^{- x^{2}}\\]","sub":"Beginner · Derivative problems","head":"Differentiate"},{"text":"\\[- 2 x e^{- x^{2}}\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer","more":{"text":"Chain rule: e^{−x²} · (−2x)","sub":"Steps"}}]},{"id":"calculus-52","sides":[{"text":"\\[x^{x}\\]","sub":"Beginner · Derivative problems","head":"Differentiate"},{"text":"\\[x^{x} \\left(\\ln{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right)\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer","more":{"text":"Log differentiation: ln y = x ln x\ny′/y = ln x + 1\ny′ = xˣ(ln x + 1)","sub":"Steps"}}]},{"id":"calculus-53","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\arctan{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}\\]","sub":"Beginner · Derivative problems","head":"Differentiate"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{2 x}{x^{4} + 1}\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer","more":{"text":"Chain rule: 1/(1+(x²)²) · 2x\n= 2x/(1+x⁴)","sub":"Steps"}}]},{"id":"calculus-54","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\tan^{3}{\\left(x \\right)}\\]","sub":"Beginner · Derivative problems","head":"Differentiate"},{"text":"\\[3\\tan^2x\\sec^2x\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer","more":{"text":"Chain rule: 3tan²x · (tan x)′\n= 3tan²x sec²x","sub":"Steps"}}]},{"id":"calculus-55","sides":[{"text":"\\(y=x^2\\) at x=3","sub":"Beginner · Derivative problems","head":"Tangent line"},{"text":"\\[y=6x-9\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer","more":{"text":"Slope 2·3=6, point (3,9): y−9=6(x−3).","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-56","sides":[{"text":"Linearization","sub":"Beginner · Derivative problems"},{"text":"\\(L(x)=f(a)+f'(a)(x-a)\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Estimate √4.1 ≈ 2+(1/4)(0.1)=2.025.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-57","sides":[{"text":"Differentials","sub":"Beginner · Derivative problems"},{"text":"\\(dy=f'(x)\\,dx\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"calculus-58","sides":[{"text":"Mean Value Theorem","sub":"Beginner · Applications of derivatives"},{"text":"\\(f'(c)=\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Needs f continuous on [a,b], differentiable on (a,b). Some point has the average slope. Rolle's theorem is the case f(a)=f(b).","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-59","sides":[{"text":"Critical numbers","sub":"Beginner · Applications of derivatives"},{"text":"f'(c)=0 or f'(c) does not exist (c in the domain)","sub":""}]},{"id":"calculus-60","sides":[{"text":"First derivative test","sub":"Beginner · Applications of derivatives"},{"text":"f' changes + to − ⇒ local max; − to + ⇒ local min; no change ⇒ neither","sub":""}]},{"id":"calculus-61","sides":[{"text":"Second derivative test","sub":"Beginner · Applications of derivatives"},{"text":"f'(c)=0: f''(c)>0 ⇒ min; f''(c)<0 ⇒ max; f''(c)=0 inconclusive","sub":"","more":{"text":"f'' > 0 means concave up; inflection points are where concavity changes.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-62","sides":[{"text":"Absolute extrema on [a,b]","sub":"Beginner · Applications of derivatives"},{"text":"Compare f at critical numbers and at the endpoints","sub":"","more":{"text":"Extreme Value Theorem guarantees they exist for continuous f on a closed interval.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-63","sides":[{"text":"Optimization recipe","sub":"Beginner · Applications of derivatives"},{"text":"Draw, define variable, write objective and constraint, reduce to one variable, find critical points, check endpoints","sub":"","more":{"text":"Example: fence 200 ft for max rectangle ⇒ a square, 50×50.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-64","sides":[{"text":"Related rates recipe","sub":"Beginner · Applications of derivatives"},{"text":"Relate the quantities, differentiate w.r.t. t, then substitute known values","sub":"","more":{"text":"Ladder: x²+y²=L² ⇒ x x' + y y' = 0. Substitute only after differentiating.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-65","sides":[{"text":"Newton's method","sub":"Beginner · Applications of derivatives"},{"text":"\\(x_{n+1}=x_n-\\frac{f(x_n)}{f'(x_n)}\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Quadratic convergence near a simple root. Fails if f'(x_n)≈0.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-66","sides":[{"text":"Position, velocity, acceleration","sub":"Beginner · Applications of derivatives"},{"text":"\\(v=s',\\ a=v'=s''\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Speed is |v|. Particle speeds up when v and a have the same sign.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-67","sides":[{"text":"Velocity of ball: \\(s=-16t^2+64t\\)","sub":"Beginner · Applications of derivatives"},{"text":"Peak at t=2 s, height 64 ft","sub":"","more":{"text":"v=−32t+64=0 ⇒ t=2.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-68","sides":[{"text":"Riemann sum definition","sub":"Beginner · Integrals"},{"text":"\\(\\int_a^bf\\,dx=\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\sum_{i=1}^nf(x_i^*)\\Delta x\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Δx=(b−a)/n. Area under the curve as rectangles thin out.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-69","sides":[{"text":"Fundamental Theorem of Calculus, part 1","sub":"Beginner · Integrals"},{"text":"\\(\\frac{d}{dx}\\int_a^xf(t)\\,dt=f(x)\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"With chain rule: d/dx ∫_a^{g(x)} f = f(g(x)) g'(x).","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-70","sides":[{"text":"Fundamental Theorem of Calculus, part 2","sub":"Beginner · Integrals"},{"text":"\\(\\int_a^bf\\,dx=F(b)-F(a)\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"F is any antiderivative of f.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-71","sides":[{"text":"Average value of a function","sub":"Beginner · Integrals"},{"text":"\\(f_{avg}=\\frac1{b-a}\\int_a^bf\\,dx\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"calculus-72","sides":[{"text":"Properties of definite integrals","sub":"Beginner · Integrals"},{"text":"Reversing limits flips sign; ∫_a^a = 0; splits at any c; linear","sub":""}]},{"id":"calculus-73","sides":[{"text":"Even/odd symmetry on [−a,a]","sub":"Beginner · Integrals"},{"text":"\\(\\text{odd: }\\int=0;\\ \\text{even: }2\\int_0^a\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"calculus-74","sides":[{"text":"Substitution rule","sub":"Beginner · Integrals"},{"text":"\\(\\int f(g(x))g'(x)\\,dx=\\int f(u)\\,du\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"For definite integrals, change the limits to u-values.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-75","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\int a^x\\,dx\\]","sub":"Beginner · Integrals","head":"Integrate"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{a^x}{\\ln a}+C\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer"}]},{"id":"calculus-76","sides":[{"text":"Antiderivative table: \\(\\int x^n dx\\)","sub":"Beginner · Integrals"},{"text":"\\(\\frac{x^{n+1}}{n+1}+C\\ (n\\ne-1)\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"calculus-77","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\int\\frac1x dx\\]","sub":"Beginner · Integrals","head":"Integrate"},{"text":"\\[\\ln|x|+C\\]","sub":"","head":"Answer"}]},{"id":"calculus-78","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\int \\sin x\\,dx\\]","sub":"Beginner · Integrals","head":"Integrate"},{"text":"\\(- \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\)\\(+C\\)","sub":"","head":"Answer"}]},{"id":"calculus-79","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\int \\cos x\\,dx\\]","sub":"Beginner · Integrals","head":"Integrate"},{"text":"\\(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}\\)\\(+C\\)","sub":"","head":"Answer"}]},{"id":"calculus-80","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\int \\sec^2x\\,dx\\]","sub":"Beginner · Integrals","head":"Integrate"},{"text":"\\(\\frac{\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}}{\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}}\\)\\(+C\\)","sub":"","head":"Answer"}]},{"id":"calculus-81","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\int \\sec x\\tan x\\,dx\\]","sub":"Beginner · Integrals","head":"Integrate"},{"text":"\\(\\frac{1}{\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}}\\)\\(+C\\)","sub":"","head":"Answer"}]},{"id":"calculus-82","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\int e^x\\,dx\\]","sub":"Beginner · Integrals","head":"Integrate"},{"text":"\\(e^{x}\\)\\(+C\\)","sub":"","head":"Answer"}]},{"id":"calculus-83","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\int \\frac1{1+x^2}\\,dx\\]","sub":"Beginner · Integrals","head":"Integrate"},{"text":"\\(\\arctan{\\left(x \\right)}\\)\\(+C\\)","sub":"","head":"Answer"}]},{"id":"calculus-84","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\int \\frac1{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}\\,dx\\]","sub":"Beginner · Integrals","head":"Integrate"},{"text":"\\(\\arcsin{\\left(x \\right)}\\)\\(+C\\)","sub":"","head":"Answer"}]},{"id":"calculus-85","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\int \\tan x\\,dx\\]","sub":"Beginner · Integrals","head":"Integrate"},{"text":"\\(- \\ln{\\left(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)} \\right)}\\)\\(+C\\)","sub":"","head":"Answer"}]},{"id":"calculus-86","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\int \\sec x\\,dx\\]","sub":"Beginner · Integrals","head":"Integrate"},{"text":"\\(- \\frac{\\ln{\\left(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - 1 \\right)}}{2} + \\frac{