inθ · √(a²+x²): x=a tanθ · √(x²−a²): x=a secθ","sub":""}]},{"id":"calculus-107","sides":[{"text":"Powers of sine and cosine","sub":"Intermediate · Integration techniques"},{"text":"Odd power: save one factor, convert the rest with sin²+cos²=1. Even powers: half-angle formulas.","sub":""}]},{"id":"calculus-108","sides":[{"text":"Half-angle identities","sub":"Intermediate · Integration techniques"},{"text":"\\(\\sin^2x=\\frac{1-\\cos2x}2,\\ \\cos^2x=\\frac{1+\\cos2x}2\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"calculus-109","sides":[{"text":"Partial fractions","sub":"Intermediate · Integration techniques"},{"text":"Factor the denominator. Linear: A/(x−a). Repeated: A/(x−a)+B/(x−a)². Irreducible quadratic: (Ax+B)/(x²+bx+c). Improper: divide first.","sub":""}]},{"id":"calculus-110","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\int \\frac{1}{x^{2} - 1}\\,dx\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Integration techniques","head":"Integrate"},{"text":"\\(\\frac{\\ln{\\left(x - 1 \\right)}}{2} - \\frac{\\ln{\\left(x + 1 \\right)}}{2}\\)\\(+C\\)","sub":"","head":"Answer","more":{"text":"Partial fractions: 1/(x²−1) = ½[1/(x−1) − 1/(x+1)]\nIntegrate each: ½ ln|(x−1)/(x+1)|","sub":"Steps"}}]},{"id":"calculus-111","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\int \\frac{3 x + 5}{\\left(x + 1\\right) \\left(x^{2} + 1\\right)}\\,dx\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Integration techniques","head":"Integrate"},{"text":"\\(\\ln{\\left(x + 1 \\right)} - \\frac{\\ln{\\left(x^{2} + 1 \\right)}}{2} + 4 \\arctan{\\left(x \\right)}\\)\\(+C\\)","sub":"","head":"Answer","more":{"text":"Partial fractions: A/(x+1) + (Bx+C)/(x²+1)\nA=1, B=−1, C=4\nln|x+1| − ½ln(x²+1) + 4 arctan x","sub":"Steps"}}]},{"id":"calculus-112","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\int \\frac{1}{x^{2} \\left(x + 1\\right)}\\,dx\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Integration techniques","head":"Integrate"},{"text":"\\(- \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} + \\ln{\\left(x + 1 \\right)} - \\frac{1}{x}\\)\\(+C\\)","sub":"","head":"Answer","more":{"text":"Partial fractions: −1/x + 1/x² + 1/(x+1)\nln|x+1| − ln|x| − 1/x + C","sub":"Steps"}}]},{"id":"calculus-113","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\int \\sqrt{1 - x^{2}}\\,dx\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Integration techniques","head":"Integrate"},{"text":"\\(\\frac{x \\sqrt{1 - x^{2}}}{2} + \\frac{\\arcsin{\\left(x \\right)}}{2}\\)\\(+C\\)","sub":"","head":"Answer","more":{"text":"Trig substitution x = sin θ, dx = cos θ dθ\n∫cos²θ dθ = θ/2 + sin2θ/4\nBack-substitute θ = arcsin x","sub":"Steps"}}]},{"id":"calculus-114","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\int \\frac{1}{x^{2} \\sqrt{x^{2} + 9}}\\,dx\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Integration techniques","head":"Integrate"},{"text":"\\(- \\frac{\\sqrt{x^{2} + 9}}{9 x}\\)\\(+C\\)","sub":"","head":"Answer","more":{"text":"Trig substitution x = 3 tan θ\n∫ sec θ/(9 tan²θ)... = (1/9)∫cos θ/sin²θ dθ\n= −√(x²+9)/(9x) + C","sub":"Steps"}}]},{"id":"calculus-115","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\int \\sin^{3}{\\left(x \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(x \\right)}\\,dx\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Integration techniques","head":"Integrate"},{"text":"\\(\\frac{\\cos^{5}{\\left(x \\right)}}{5} - \\frac{\\cos^{3}{\\left(x \\right)}}{3}\\)\\(+C\\)","sub":"","head":"Answer","more":{"text":"Odd power of sine: save one sin x, sin²x = 1 − cos²x\nu = cos x: −∫(1−u²)u² du\n= −cos³x/3 + cos⁵x/5 + C","sub":"Steps"}}]},{"id":"calculus-116","sides":[{"text":"Improper integral: infinite limit","sub":"Intermediate · Integration techniques"},{"text":"\\(\\int_a^\\infty f=\\lim_{b\\to\\infty}\\int_a^bf\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"calculus-117","sides":[{"text":"p-test for integrals","sub":"Intermediate · Integration techniques"},{"text":"\\(\\int_1^\\infty x^{-p}dx\\text{ converges iff }p>1\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Near 0: ∫_0^1 x^{-p} converges iff p<1.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"calculus-118","sides":[{"text":"Comparison test for integrals","sub":"Intermediate · Integration techniques"},{"text":"0≤f≤g: ∫g converges ⇒ ∫f converges; ∫f diverges ⇒ ∫g diverges","sub":""}]},{"id":"calculus-119","sides":[{"text":"\\[\\int_0^\\infty e^{-x}dx\\]","sub":"Intermediate · Integration techniques","head":"Integrat